              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "I ran each tool once, since repeating the calls wouldn't add anything new. Here's a summary of what they returned.\n\n**Profile:** Alberto Carbonell is a Senior Software Engineer (AI Agents & Full-Stack TypeScript) based in Spain, working remotely. He has 10+ years with TypeScript, Node.js and PostgreSQL, and lately builds AI agents that handle real work end to end. He holds a CFGS in Web Development, Multiplatform Development and Systems Administration (CIFP Rodolfo Ucha Piñeiro, 2010–2015). He speaks Spanish (native) and English (C1).\n\n**Experience:**\n- **CoverWallet**, Senior Software Engineer, 2019–now. Insurtech platform. Leads cross-team projects, integrates insurance carrier APIs, and introduced AI agents into the engineering workflow.\n- **M&GT Consulting**, Software Developer, 2016–2019. REST APIs, web and mobile apps, and blockchain work on Hyperledger Fabric and Ethereum.\n- **Indra**, Software Developer, 2015–2016. Java/Spring and Oracle PL/SQL for telecom clients.\n\n**AI agent projects:**\n- **Fraud Detection Agent** (offline evals). Reviews new events and organizers on a ticketing platform and recommends approve, reject or request info. In evals, Claude Haiku 5.5 was chosen for deployment, with 86% accuracy and 1% of fraud approved.\n- **Organizer Support Agent** (coming soon). Answers organizer questions about sales, payouts and setup using live data.\n- **Portfolio Agent** (personal project). The assistant you're chatting with now, also exposed as an MCP server.\n\n**Stack:** Claude, tool calling, MCP and agent evals on the AI side. TypeScript, JavaScript and Ruby. Node.js, NestJS, Next.js, PostgreSQL and MongoDB on the backend. Docker, Kubernetes, GCP and others on infra. React, React Native and Angular on the frontend.\n\nFor availability, rates or anything else not covered here, you can reach him through the contact details on his site."
              }
